# Settings and Control Panel

## Settings

- Modern Windows settings tool
- Easier and user-friendly
- Used for common system changes

## Control Panel

- Traditional Windows management tool
- Used for advanced settings
- Can manage programs, network, accounts, etc. 

## Accessing Them

- Open from Start Menu
- Search directly from Windows Search

# Network Settings Example

- Settings → Network & Internet
- Click Change adapter options
- Opens Control Panel network settings

# Windows Search

- Search settings quickly from Start Menu
- Example:
  - Search "wallpaper" to change background

# Task Manager

- Shows running apps and processes
- Displays:
  - CPU usage
  - RAM usage
  - Background processes

## Opening Task Manager

- Right-click taskbar → Task Manager
- Shortcut:
  - Ctrl + Shift + Esc

## Views

### Simple View

- Shows open applications only

### Detailed View

- Shows:
  - Processes
  - Performance
  - Users
  - Services
  - Details

# Important Use of Task Manager

- End unresponsive apps
- Monitor system performance
- Check memory and CPU usage
